== an unset name near a set name names it:
1:23: warning: The variable 'output_fil' is never assigned, and 'output_file' is.
     1 |  output_file=out; echo "$output_fil"
       |                        ^~~~~~~~~~~~~
1:1: details:
     1 |  output_file=out; echo "$output_fil"
       |  ^~~~~~~~~~~~~~~ the assignment that gives 'output_file' a value runs here.
note: Correct the spelling or assign 'output_fil'.
1:24: warning: The variable 'output_fil' is not set, it expands to empty.
     1 |  output_file=out; echo "$output_fil"
       |                         ^~~~~~~~~~~
note: The variable 'output_file' is set, correct the spelling, or replace this with ${output_fil-} if empty expansion is desired.

== a transposed pair names the set name:
1:29: warning: The variable 'destinaton_path' is never assigned, and 'destination_path' is.
     1 |  destination_path=/tmp; echo "$destinaton_path"
       |                              ^~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
1:1: details:
     1 |  destination_path=/tmp; echo "$destinaton_path"
       |  ^~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~ the assignment that gives 'destination_path' a value runs here.
note: Correct the spelling or assign 'destinaton_path'.
1:30: warning: The variable 'destinaton_path' is not set, it expands to empty.
     1 |  destination_path=/tmp; echo "$destinaton_path"
       |                               ^~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
note: The variable 'destination_path' is set, correct the spelling, or replace this with ${destinaton_path-} if empty expansion is desired.

== a name far from every set name keeps the plain note:
1:29: warning: The variable 'zzzzzzzzzzzzzz' is read before any assignment gives it a value.
     1 |  destination_path=/tmp; echo "$zzzzzzzzzzzzzz"
       |                              ^~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
note: Assign 'zzzzzzzzzzzzzz' before it is read, or export it from the environment.
1:30: warning: The variable 'zzzzzzzzzzzzzz' is not set, it expands to empty.
     1 |  destination_path=/tmp; echo "$zzzzzzzzzzzzzz"
       |                               ^~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
note: Replace it with ${zzzzzzzzzzzzzz-} if empty expansion is desired.

== nounset names the set name in its fatal note:
1:39: error: The variable 'configuration_rot' is never assigned, and 'configuration_root' is.
     1 |  set -u; configuration_root=/etc; echo "$configuration_rot"
       |                                        ^~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
1:9: details:
     1 |  set -u; configuration_root=/etc; echo "$configuration_rot"
       |          ^~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~ the assignment that gives 'configuration_root' a value runs here.
note: Correct the spelling or assign 'configuration_rot'.
rc=1
== an exported name is a candidate:
1:7: warning: The variable 'KOSH_TEST_EXPORTE' is not set, it expands to empty.
     1 |  echo "$KOSH_TEST_EXPORTE"
       |        ^~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
note: The variable 'KOSH_TEST_EXPORTED' is set, correct the spelling, or replace this with ${KOSH_TEST_EXPORTE-} if empty expansion is desired.

